        ],
        "reason": "Native Content-Length short reads are accumulated until an empty read; a nonzero remaining HTTPResponse.length then creates a framing failure before JSON decoding. Thus a syntactically valid JSON prefix cannot be admitted merely because bounded read returned without exception. Complete nonempty bodies receive complete only after the read loop observes native completion, unless the cap instead produces captured_prefix. Empty bodies retain unavailable identity. The corrected fixtures construct actual HTTPResponse objects rather than relying only on BytesIO."
      },
      {
        "id": "L2",
        "disposition": "resolved_by_source_inspection",
        "sources": [
          "tools/fetch-candles.py:411-438,472-506,585-607,701-722",
          "test/fixtures/fetch-candles-provenance.py:64-79,91-132"
        ],
        "reason": "IncompleteRead is caught at the read producer before the broader HTTPException handler. Exposed partial bytes are appended to previously returned bytes and fingerprinted without text persistence. Read-time HTTPException/OSError faults become named framing failures; open-time HTTPException becomes a named request failure. Retry exhaustion returns Unavailable into recorded_get, attempt persistence and whole-source fallback. Missing standard-library-internal bytes are explicitly unknown rather than fabricated."
      }
    ],
